#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:5
#: c140a806b6eb4763a660c37bd6accbfa
msgid "Setting Home and/or EKF origin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:7
#: 51f6573d672c4e268362cd2be4c0243f
msgid "This page explains how MAVLink can be used by a ground station or companion computer to get or set the home or EKF origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:10
#: eb7c8b82300241a2946128489bb2e59f
msgid "Home vs EKF Origin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:12
#: ea5a5a8a776745139501836a6085e8a7
msgid "The vehicles \"Home\" position is the location (specified as a latitude, longitude and altitude above sea level) that the vehicle will return to in :ref:`RTL <copter:rtl-mode>` mode.  For most vehicles this location is set to the vehicle's current location each time the vehicle is armed but it may also be moved at any time.  Moving home can be useful in situations where the user wishes RTL mode to return the vehicle to a different location than it took off from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:14
#: f97d353cf5654fe291ae72b5b05427a8
msgid "The \"EKF origin\" is the location that the EKF (aka AHRS) uses for internal calculations.  This location is normally set to the vehicle's location soon after the GPS provides a good quality location.  Once set the EKF origin cannot be moved.  Users are not normally aware of the EKF origin's location unless they are using Non-GPS navigation on a vehicle with no GPS attached (without a GPS, the user must specify the EKF origin using the ground station)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:16
#: 79ae34f710f04cba992b6daf64dfe138
msgid "Whenever the Home or EKF origin is updated the vehicle will send a `HOME_POSITION <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#HOME_POSITION>`__ or `GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN>`__ message (respectively) on all active mavlink channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:18
#: edaccd9eaa19436ca7f9005ea0dfc171
msgid "The home will also be sent in response to a `MAV_CMD_GET_HOME_POSITION <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#MAV_CMD_GET_HOME_POSITION>`__ sent within a `COMMAND_LONG <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#COMMAND_LONG>`__ or `COMMAND_INT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#COMMAND_INT>`__ message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:23
#: a5ed0ba5c37a434da3052a70bf94363f
msgid "MAV_CMD_DO_SET_HOME within COMMAND_INT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-get-set-home-and-origin.rst:25
#: c89055ff539a4be3acfc7337658cf769
msgid "Set the home location by sending a `COMMAND_INT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#COMMAND_INT>`__ with the command and parameter fields set as specified for the `MAV_CMD_DO_SET_HOME <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#MAV_CMD_DO_SET_HOME>`__ command."
msgstr ""

